After a few months of playing, getting spoiled rotten, descending a
Barbarian to the Sanctum (where he proptly got butchered by the
Priestess of Moloch) and a Samurai to the Castle (where he got greedy
and choked on a lump of royal jelly) I decided to play the same class
for a while and try to ascend it. Turns out that was a good idea.

Our heroine began at dungeon level 1, as so many others. There she
found a co-aligned altar. This streak would last, and there were too
many co-aligned altars to remember, but the most notable one was close
to the Castle (good for stashing) and Minetown (that's always nice).

What the RNG was more stingy with was bags of holding. Our heroine
walked down... and down... and down and never found any. After finding
the entrance to the Wizard of Yendor's tower she got fed up and
extracted one from her wand of wishing. Then it was only a matter of
finding the Vibrating Square, enchanting armor beyond all reason,
sacrificing some (finally acquiring Grayswandir after using the trusty
Excalibur for most of the game).

This time, the High Priestess was introduced to a wand of death and
the Amulet was promptly grabbed. The Mysterious Force proceeded to
play with our heroine as she crossed the lairs of Asmodeus and
Baalzebub four or five times over. Juiblex's swamp got fewer visits,
and there was much rejoicing as she reached the Castle again.

The trip to the first level was relatively uneventful. Our heroine
decided to bring the artifacts she had found with her to her ascension
- including Grimtooth which rewarded this by blasting her with energy.
Unappreciative little dagger, that.

The planes weren't much more exciting. Our heroine knew the spell
"create monster" which she couldn't cast but which could at least
befuddle her enough to cast "confused scroll of gold detection". A
metric ton of wands got her past Earth (digging) and Air
(teleportation). Fire was easily crossed, and a well-timed genocide of
team ; got her past Water without much hassle.

A ring of conflict had helped in Air, and it helped at the Astral
plane too. The second try was the correct altar, and our heroine
promptly sacrificed the Amulet of Yendor...
